I think that I&#39;ve got it. &nbsp;With a round to spare, actually!

&nbsp;

The important thing is not how you kill them, but who you kill.

&nbsp;

 I&#39;ve included the general idea below in white.&nbsp; 

 [color=white]  The key is to kill Set as soon as possible. &nbsp;Set&#39;s incap effectively gives you an extra half-turn every turn, and helps you really pump out the damage.[/color] 

&nbsp;

 [color=white]  If you want more advice, this is what I did. &nbsp;Other routes will give you victory, as long as you&#39;re getting those extra plays off of Set:  [/color] 

&nbsp;

 [color=white]  Don&#39;t worry about Legacy&#39;s ring and charge - just get out inspiring presence and then Smash, Strike, and Thokk your way to glory.  [/color] 

 [color=white] Wraith can use her three Inventive Preparations to get almost fully set up in the first turn. &nbsp;I went with Razor Ordinence, Throwing Knives, Microtargetting Computer, and Utility belt the first turn and dropped Combat Stance on the second. &nbsp;Then I just Throat Jabbed until those were out, and then dropped random equiptment in anticipation of an inventory barrage at the end that I didn&#39;t actually end up needing. [/color] 

 [color=white] Parse also sets up quickly with a double&nbsp;Syntactic Analysis, which I used to get Snap Decision, a Critical Multiplier, and Recompile. &nbsp;Then I Recompiled twice more, then and started wailing with Between the Lines (for Wraith) and Impossible Shot. &nbsp;I also tossed in another critical multiplier, which probably should have gone before the second two recompiles, but whatever. &nbsp;I was hoping that with Isis&#39;s Incap I could draw out Parse&#39;s entire deck and force a reshuffle, which would have given me back the Syntactic Analyses and the Recompiles (which would have been 1 play for 27 damage if the Critical Multipliers were all out), but they turned out not to be necessary. [/color] 

 [color=white] For Villain plays, I started out with The Grave Beckons and Death&#39;s Grasp, with the occasional Sun&#39;s Fury thrown in for maximum Combat Stancing. &nbsp;None of them do very much damage, none of them harm your board, and purple tends to trigger the least harmful Ennead effects.

 [/color]
